## Summary
The number of elementary, middle, and high school students in South Korea has reached an all-time low of 5.36 million, reflecting a significant demographic shift. In contrast, students with a migration background have hit an all-time high, indicating increasing diversity in the student population. These trends suggest potential impacts on education policy and resources in the country.

## Key Points
- Total student enrollment in South Korea has dropped to a record low of 5.36 million.
- Enrollment for students with migration backgrounds has increased to a record high.
- The data highlights ongoing demographic changes affecting the educational system.
- These statistics may inform future education planning and policy decisions.


